	(text "F1 PTC RXEF030: 72 V, hold 0.30 A / trip 0.60 A at 20 C (hold ~0.20 A at 60 C), pitch 5.1 mm; alternative\n0ZRE0033FF1A (240 V, 0.33/0.74 A) fits the same holes. Both:\na SLOW, temperature dependent limiter for a shorted D1/U1, not a fast fuse. Unit draw < 0.2 A from 24 V.\nD1 P6KE47CA (bidirectional, DO-15): standoff 40.2 V > 29 V, clamp 64.8 V < 72 V TSR max (as SMAJ40A in D1).\nU1 TRACO TSR 1-4850WI 9-72 V -> 5 V / 1 A, SIP-3 (1 = IN, 2 = GND, 3 = OUT) + 2 case pins, body 12.1x8.6x17.5 mm;\nno tracks under the converter (TRACO drawing rev. 2026-07-02, review E-01).\nD2 1N5819: the DevKit must not get 5 V from both the 5V pin and its USB at once (Espressif: 'mutually\nexclusive') - the diode keeps the USB 5 V out of the TSR. DevKit 5V pin ~4.6 V is enough for its LDO.\n+3V3 = the DevKit's own 3.3 V regulator (3V3 pins): pull-ups, NTC dividers, I2C / 1-Wire sensors."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154 92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cb98b99c-be32-50f5-9b6f-e33784a98c90")
	)
